==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|anti|coagulant}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|medicine}} A substance that prevents [[coagulation]] (stops blood from [[clot]]ting); especially, any of a group of pharmaceutical drugs that reduce the [[clotting]] speed or affinity of the blood by any of several mechanisms (e.g., inhibiting [[platelet]] function, inhibiting [[clotting factor]] (protein) production or function, increasing [[antithrombin]] function).
#: {{syn|en|blood thinner<qq:informal>}}
#: {{ant|en|coagulant|;|styptic}}
#: {{hypo|en|q=1platelet function|aspirin|q2=clotting factors|warfarin|dicoumarol|acenocoumarol|apixaban|dabigatran|q7=antithrombin|heparin}}

